@startuml SequenceAiGenerate
' Scenario 3 — Generating an exam with the AI agent
' Shows validation of untrusted model output and the fallback path.

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 210

actor Teacher
participant "GenerateExamPage" as Page
box "Server" #F8FAFC
  participant "aiController" as Ctrl
  participant "AiService" as Svc
  participant "NimProvider" as Nim
  participant "FallbackProvider" as Fall
  participant "ExamService" as Exams
end box
participant "NVIDIA NIM\n(external)" as Cloud
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

Teacher -> Page : describes the exam\n"CSS flexbox, 4 questions"
Page -> Ctrl : POST /api/ai/exams/generate
Ctrl -> Svc : generateExam({description, questionCount})

Svc -> Svc : clamp questionCount to 1..20

alt an API key is configured
  Svc -> Nim : generateExam(spec)
  Nim -> Cloud : POST /chat/completions\nsystem prompt + JSON schema
  Cloud --> Nim : completion text
  Nim -> Nim : parseJsonReply()
  note right of Nim
    Models fence JSON in markdown even when
    told not to, so the reply is unwrapped
    before parsing rather than trusted.
  end note
  Nim --> Svc : raw exam object
else no key, OR the provider failed
  Svc -> Fall : generateExam(spec)
  note right of Fall
    Unreachable, model retired (410),
    timeout, or unparseable reply all land
    here. The feature degrades; it does
    not fail.
  end note
  Fall --> Svc : template exam
end

Svc -> Svc : validate the shape
note right of Svc
  A model's output is UNTRUSTED INPUT.
  Repairable: weights that do not total 100.
  Rejected: a multiple-choice question with
  one option, or a correct answer pointing
  outside the options — either would violate
  a CHECK constraint and surface as a 500.
end note

alt validation fails
  Svc -> Fall : generateExam(spec)
  Fall --> Svc : template exam
  Svc -> Svc : validate again
end

Svc --> Ctrl : { exam, generatedBy, modelBacked }
Ctrl --> Page : 200

note over Page, DB
  NOTHING HAS BEEN SAVED.
  The draft is returned for review, because a
  generated answer key can be confident and
  wrong — observed three times in testing.
end note

Page -> Teacher : shows the draft, badged with the provider,\nwith a warning to check every answer

Teacher -> Page : reviews, edits, clicks Save
Page -> Exams : POST /api/exams { ..., generatedByAi: true, aiPrompt }
Exams -> DB : INSERT exam + questions
note right of DB
  Provenance is recorded, so the UI can badge
  the exam and the teacher can see the prompt
  it came from.
end note
Exams --> Page : the created exam (status: Draft)
Page -> Teacher : opens the editor for final changes

@enduml
